docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/scoping-8d.3.md:43:### D. `Voyager.build_route` compat shim disposition
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/scoping-8d.3.md:47:- **D2.** Rename to `Voyager.build_route_for_static_site` to make intent clear.
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/scoping-8d.3.md:57:- Web has TWO modes: (i) static-site (Voyager's path; uses `Voyager.build_route` shim); (ii) full Amber server (Phase 8C's `routes_for(UI::App)`; proven on `samples/phase-08-amber-spike/`).
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/scoping-8d.3.md:111:### Item 5 — `Voyager.build_route` shim disposition
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/codex-critique-1-brief-8d.1.md:14:### 1. BLOCKER — `Voyager.build_route` removal breaks iOS + web
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/codex-critique-1-brief-8d.1.md:16:Brief Item 1 removes `Voyager.build_route` but `web/static_site.cr` AND `ios/bridge.cr` both call it. iOS is explicitly out of 8D.1 scope; web is too (per Codex co-plan B2 — web stays static). Removing the method breaks compile/link for both targets during the 8D.1 → 8D.2 window.
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/codex-critique-1-brief-8d.1.md:18:**Resolution:** Keep `Voyager.build_route(state, coord, route)` as a temporary COMPATIBILITY SHIM in 8D.1. The shim constructs a minimal `UI::ScreenContext::Native` (without dispatcher integration), looks up the screen class via `VoyagerApp.registration_for(route.id).screen_class`, and calls `screen.build(ctx)`. This is the bridge that keeps iOS + web compiling while the macOS host migrates fully. 8D.2 (iOS bridge migration) is the phase that removes the shim.
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/codex-critique-1-brief-8d.1.md:94:Brief said "REPLACE the `Voyager.build_route` / `Voyager.route_for_slug` / `Voyager.slug_for_route_id` module methods" then said "Remove `build_route`; keep `route_for_slug` + `slug_for_route_id`."
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/codex-critique-1-brief-8d.1.md:96:**Resolution:** Brief v2 says: keep `Voyager.build_route` as a temporary compat shim (per Finding 1); keep `route_for_slug` + `slug_for_route_id` unchanged.
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/scoping-8d.2.md:12:Phase 8D.1 migrated Voyager's macOS host to `UI::ActionDispatcher`. The iOS bridge at `samples/initiative-cross-platform-ui-voyager/ios/bridge.cr` still calls the `Voyager.build_route(state, coord, route)` **compat shim**, which constructs a dispatcher-less `ScreenContext::Native`. As a result:
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/scoping-8d.2.md:54:Today's `render_slug` calls `Voyager.build_route(state, coord, route)`. After 8D.2 it must:
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/scoping-8d.2.md:94:- `Voyager.build_route` is still called by `samples/initiative-cross-platform-ui-voyager/web/static_site.cr`.
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/brief-8d.3a.md:16:Close the long-deferred Save-enabled-on-type behavioral bug in `TodoEditorScreen` AND run the owner hand-test gate that 8D.1 + 8D.2 both deferred. Resolve the `Voyager.build_route` web shim disposition to D1 (keep, doc). Commit the B2 web architecture position note.
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/brief-8d.3a.md:31:- **No `Voyager.build_route` rename or migration.**
docs/initiative-cross-platform-ui/phases/phase-08-ergonomic-mvc-api/brief-8d.3a.md:154:### Item 5 — `Voyager.build_route` D1 disposition + comprehensive comment cleanup (per Codex LOW 1)
